  - **Incorrect.** The corticospinal tract is **ipsilateral** (crosses in the medulla), so weakness would be on the **same side** as the lesion.
- **(D) Right-sided analgesia**
  - **Correct.** The spinothalamic tract carries pain/temperature sensation and decussates near its entry level. A **left C5 hemicord lesion** would cause **contralateral (right-sided) loss of pain and temperature sensation** below the lesion.
- **(E) Contralateral loss of vibration and proprioception**
  - **Incorrect.** The dorsal columns (vibration/proprioception) are **ipsilateral** (cross in the medulla), so loss would be on the **same side** as the lesion.

