A hemicord lesion at **C5** (which is in the cervical spinal cord) will disrupt:
1. **Corticospinal tract (lateral funiculus)** → **Ipsilateral (left) motor weakness** (spastic paralysis below the lesion).
2. **Spinothalamic tract (anterior/lateral funiculus)** → **Contralateral (right) loss of pain and temperature sensation** (analgesia and thermoanesthesia).
