#### **(B) An increase in left ventricular end-diastolic pressure (LVEDP)**
- **Incorrect.** Standing **reduces preload**, so **LVEDP decreases** (not increases). LVEDP is directly related to LV filling volume.

#### **(C) An increase in pulmonary capillary wedge pressure (PCWP)**
- **Incorrect.** PCWP reflects **left atrial pressure (LAP)**, which is influenced by LV filling. Since standing **reduces preload**, PCWP **decreases** (not increases).

